Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:10:51

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:01:27

The app is on bc250_core (owner's decision, for consistency with the suite's apps): INFO (AppInfo) in __init__, core's create_app and exec_app in __main__ (the same names, Fusion style, icon and SIGTERM handling; core's rounded tooltips and the Inter title font are new), core's single instance, the first line built with AppHeader, and the settings opened with open_settings (the same ~/.config/bazzite-netcatgui/bazzite-netcatgui.ini). The gray subtitle under the title went: the header has the title row and one row of controls, the buttons. A second launch with a host and port or -l port opens that tab in the open window (own_arguments and open_tab in __main__, also used at start-up). install.sh bundles bc250_core from the suite checkout like the other core apps; a release has it bundled. --version names the core. Tests: the arguments a second launch hands over, and the tab they open.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 01:18:28

The app is part of the BC250 Bazzite Suite, as apps/bazzite-netcatgui, listed in the portal under "Development only". Its manual is the suite manual's chapter docs/apps/bazzite-netcatgui.md (bundled in a release as MANUAL.md), with the Install section for the portal and the suite's releases; the README links to it. The files of the standalone repository went to the suite: CLAUDE.md (the porting notes and where the work stands are in the suite's MIGRATION.md), test.sh, tools/check_versions.py and tools/fix-modes.sh (the suite's own do the same), tools/make_logo.py (the logo stays as images/bazzite-netcatgui.png and -128.png), and .gitattributes (the suite's root one is the same file). The version starts at 0.1.0, like every app of the suite (owner's decision): VERSION and __version__ go from 1.0.0 to 0.1.0, before the first release. The license stays GPL-2.0-only (owner's decision). The installer and the code are unchanged; the README's "Shinnokt" is now "Shinnok".

Changelog: 14-10-2026 18:00:21

The manual has an Examples section with three walk-throughs: fetching a web page by hand over TLS with the HTTP template, sending a file from the board to a PC with a Listen tab, Save Received Data to File and Send File, and watching a device or sitting between a client and a server with two pipes, plus the recording and replay of a handshake.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 17:26:29

The C++ tool's TODO, the owner's shortlist, is implemented (UDP, remembered hosts and ports and Clear Log were already in): TLS on Connect tabs with a certificate question when the server's certificate cannot be verified (no TLS on Listen tabs, which would need a certificate); pipes between tabs (Session > Pipe Received Data To: what a tab receives goes out through another tab's connection, both directions when set on both tabs); file pipes (File > Send File, Ctrl+Shift+F, and Save Received Data to File, appended as it is); Reconnect Automatically (three seconds after a drop or a failure, status bar instead of dialogs, until Disconnect); the message history in the message box (Up and Down, the draft kept); Hex View (Ctrl+H, the log as a hexdump per chunk with << and >> markers, re-rendered when switched) and Hex Input (Ctrl+Shift+H); the protocol highlighter (requests and commands, status and reply lines, errors, header names; Session > Highlight Protocol Lines, on by default) and Edit > Insert Protocol Template (HTTP GET and HEAD, SMTP, POP3, IMAP, FTP, IRC, Redis, memcached; switches the tab to newline and CRLF); session recordings (File > Save Session Recording, a .ncrec.json with the bytes and the pauses) and their replay through the current tab (File > Replay Recording, the status bar counts, Disconnect stops it); Rename Tab (F2), Tab Color and the tab bar's right-click menu with Close Other Tabs. Also: the line ending now replaces the line breaks inside a multi-line message; received text is decoded incrementally, so a character split over two chunks survives; a user Disconnect flushes what was just written. Running connections in separate threads is not done on purpose: the Qt sockets are asynchronous in the event loop. The manual describes everything; 34 tests, the TLS one with a self-signed certificate from the openssl binary.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 16:44:00

Renamed without the BC250 prefix (owner's decision): the app is "Bazzite NetcatGUI", app id bazzite-netcatgui, package netcat_gui, installed to ~/.local/share/bazzite-netcatgui with the launcher bazzite-netcatgui and its settings in ~/.config/bazzite-netcatgui/bazzite-netcatgui.ini; the logo files are images/bazzite-netcatgui.png and -128.png. The repository folder is bazzite-netcatgui.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 15:50:18

First Python + Qt port of NetcatGUI 1.0 (github.com/shinnok/netcatgui, C++/Qt, GPL-2.0) for Bazzite, built like bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor: a flat package run with python -m, PyQt6, install.sh with --uninstall/--purge/--no-desktop-shortcut installing into ~/.local/share/bazzite-netcatgui with its own venv, a launcher in ~/.local/bin, a menu entry and a Desktop icon, VERSION, test.sh, tools/check_versions.py, tools/fix-modes.sh, the suite's .gitattributes, SPDX headers on every file. The window has the suite's first line: the logo at 96 px beside the title with the version, the tab buttons below it; the logo is drawn by tools/make_logo.py. Ported: Connect and Listen tabs over TCP, the Latin-1/UTF-8/System encodings, the newline option, every keyboard shortcut, Save Log with the C++ tool's header, About. Added: UDP per tab (a Listen tab answers the last sender), Clear Log, Echo Sent Messages, a Line Ending submenu (LF or CRLF; the C++ menu said CRLF and sent LF), the Session menu following the current tab, hosts and ports and the menu state remembered in the .ini, nc-like arguments (host port, -l port, -u). Differences from the C++ tool, all in CLAUDE.md and the manual: received chunks are appended without an extra line break, a peer closing the connection sets the status bar instead of a modal box, one TCP client at a time on a Listen tab, the name lookup inside the socket instead of blocking the window, Save Log in UTF-8. 19 tests over the loopback (TCP, UDP, encodings, the window, the settings) pass under PyQt6 6.11 on Windows.
